{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/coverage.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591423Z","id":"d9fc825098e182486a59f4bcc1b637b32be708233e95daffae90fab63cb4459a","body":{"detail":"jarl/proofs/consensus/project.json binds 10 theorems (majority_strict, majority_intersection, joint_commit_requires_both, follower_never_overcommits, commit_never_regresses, current_term_required, commit_sequence_monotone, and others) to slices of src/membership.rs Membership::quorum/quorum_index and src/node.rs Node::append, Node::commit_to and Node::advance_commit. No coverage.json entry references jarl/proofs/consensus/project.json. The advance_commit (line 4889), append (4903) and commit_to (5036) entries have status 'planned' and an empty contracts list. M0.md:36-37 says 'Contract references are checked against project obligation manifests', but provium::coverage::audit (provium/src/coverage.rs:485-505) checks only that each ledger reference exists in a project. It never checks the reverse, that each project obligation appears in the ledger. Evidence can therefore silently go missing from the ledger, and the ledger understates what the consensus slices cover.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4889},"end":{"line":4910},"content_hash":"abe43398749d78815a9c0ed98ecbed2a9fa605ad84173573ae1bf6d466a5809a"},"suggested_fix":"Add the consensus contracts to the advance_commit, append, commit_to and quorum entries, with notes saying they are slice-only (guarded-assignment prefix, majority comparison, min expression). Then add a test to jarl/tests/proofs.rs that fails when any obligation in any proofs/*/project.json (except the specification project) is not referenced from coverage.json.","summary":"coverage.json records none of the 10 consensus-project obligations; Node::append, commit_to and advance_commit stay 'planned' with no contracts","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/coverage.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591865Z","id":"7ef69833059093e882d9d62f301a9658327b00a4c35b9b425453d110928d73b4","body":{"detail":"State::write (src/state.rs:101) is pub(crate). The inventory marks it public=false, yet its coverage entry has root_apis [\"crate::state::<State < V , S , CAP >>::write\"]. Every other private method, such as State::full and State::get, has an empty root_apis list, and the real public root is Ready::write (src/ready.rs:51). Counting distinct root_apis gives 101, while M0.md:57 and :179 state '100 conservative roots'. The provium audit (provium/src/coverage.rs:479) checks only that public items list themselves, so it does not catch this.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":6937},"end":{"line":6950},"content_hash":"f16399228659ba60ac0cecf6aaf0b4ff5e5fc502b52dff1672485917625d88a1"},"suggested_fix":"Change the root_apis of the State::write entry to [\"crate::ready::<Ready < '_ , V , S , N , CAP >>::write\"] (or empty, as for the other private items), then refresh m0-review.json.","summary":"The pub(crate) State::write entry lists itself as a public root API, so the ledger has 101 roots against M0.md's stated 100","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.591946Z","id":"9cbf3f39811727289f76da69e7feabdcb8a71052ba2ccbd28be81d366687be40","body":{"detail":"JarlProofs.majority_intersection (jarl/proofs/consensus/Proofs.lean:43-61) quantifies over an arbitrary `voters : List α` and arbitrary pure predicates. Its own comment (lines 29-31) says the caller must still connect these to the membership iterator. The membership project proves Quorum.execution, under which Membership::quorum counts a stateful callback over the voters and old_voters projections, and the old pass receives the advanced callback handle. No Jarl theorem instantiates majority_intersection with these projections. The composition is also not immediate: the FnMut callback in src/membership.rs:166-179 may answer differently for the same identity in the two passes, and jarl/tests/proof_cases/quorum_callbacks.rs exercises repeated identities.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":45},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"a7c54ef99d24c1f6d9efc1de53e52e88f25bfd7fb316dd7b44204ed713dd4a36"},"suggested_fix":"Either reword README.md:45 to 'strict-majority intersection over abstract voter lists (not yet linked to Membership::quorum)', or add a Jarl theorem showing that two successful membership_Membership_quorum executions over the same entries, with deterministic callback answers, share a current voter (and an old voter when joint).","summary":"README claims an 'actual shared-voter intersection' for consensus, but no theorem connects the intersection lemma to the generated Membership::quorum execution","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.592080Z","id":"4430a24908ed238aabb05172ac3a5d18f4a5b86d079ce12d13b3b59e6ecba43b","body":{"detail":"jarl/proofs/membership/project.json lists 15 methods, including membership::Membership::quorum and quorum_index, with 5 Quorum.* and 9 QuorumIndex.* obligations. The README row lists only finalized, is_joint, voters, old_voters, learners, contains, is_voter, include, new/restore, peers, with_learners and joint. Readers cannot learn from it what the quorum contracts establish (execution equations, word/build refinements, response budgets) or what they leave out (majority safety).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"6dcce95a55b4bebd75c419877e31651455185ddac1c6ea9b8ab95190a5c943ee"},"suggested_fix":"Extend the README membership row to describe the quorum/quorum_index execution contracts and state explicitly that no majority-safety theorem exists yet.","summary":"The README membership row omits Membership::quorum and quorum_index, which the membership project verifies with 14 obligations","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.592290Z","id":"e7d5d47b26daff2abcc25be49a2925ce3b77456b248cb7ce0de0eb65d4817cba","body":{"detail":"AppendHistory.fresh (jarl/proofs/storage/Proofs.lean:145) and StorageHistory.fresh (Proofs.lean:943-944) are built directly as an empty buffer of replicated None slots with length 0. The generated constructor is linked only by the separate theorem fresh_representation (Proofs.lean:134-139), which the history theorems do not mention in their statements. If State::new changed (for example to `len: 1`), the history theorems would still check and only the separate obligation would fail. The comment at Proofs.lean:141-143 is also out of date: it says restore, truncation, snapshots and growth are excluded, but StorageHistory now includes all of them.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":105},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"1301d098f889206c2eaf363bf0a67804413dd5b64b904ee2132c8d1f590a3b8b"},"suggested_fix":"Give the fresh constructors a premise linking them to Jarl.state_State_new (for example a representation relation with capacity = sizes \"CAP\"), or reword README.md:105-106 to say the history starts from an empty buffer that fresh_representation separately relates to the constructor. Update the comment at Proofs.lean:141-143.","summary":"README says the append-history induction starts 'from the generated constructor', but both history inductions start from a hand-written empty buffer instead of Jarl.state_State_new","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/PROGRESS.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.592366Z","id":"d55dce27be5044711f7028386f8ccf0e888084d3cf87eb534f03d909b3004e9d","body":{"detail":"PROGRESS.md:478 and :505 say the storage project has 44 obligations, but jarl/proofs/storage/project.json declares 53, the additions being the State::hard and State::snapshot getters and grow_initialized_moves. PROGRESS.md:1269 and :1374 say the membership project checks 111, but jarl/proofs/membership/project.json lists 114, after the QuorumIndex target/build word contracts were added in later P06 sections that do not restate the total. PROGRESS.md:1384 says 'The host suite checks 267 declared method obligations', but the ten method projects now declare 284 (12+2+4+53+8+6+13+56+16+114). Because every one of these is written as a present-tense 'now' statement in a running log, readers cannot tell the current evidence scope.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":478},"end":{"line":505},"content_hash":"1320de17b8d1e9269fa1f932cf1464be8963e1e98114cfe272dbda3af20eef7b"},"suggested_fix":"Add a current-counts summary near the top of PROGRESS.md, or have a test in jarl/tests/proofs.rs assert per-project obligation counts against project.json so the documentation cannot drift. Mark older counts as historical.","summary":"PROGRESS.md gives out-of-date obligation counts in 'now has' wording (storage 44, membership 111, method suite 267) and never states the current numbers","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/coverage.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037754Z","id":"097ae5c174a513cb30f85e13bccf86c6e1c5d056c046741e23df117e051b928c","body":{"detail":"Projects referenced by coverage.json contracts: capacity 2, election 3, initialization 4, input-gating 8, log-boundary 12, membership 114, message-dispatch 2, message-validation 56, persistence 6, replication-contract 16, storage-view 13, storage 53. There are no consensus entries, and grepping coverage.json for majority_strict, joint_commit_requires_both, follower_never_overcommits, commit_never_regresses, current_term_required or commit_sequence_monotone finds nothing. jarl/proofs/consensus/project.json declares 10 obligations on slices of Membership::quorum, quorum_index, Node::append, commit_to and advance_commit. coverage.json:4889-4902 (advance_commit), 4903-4916 (append) and 5036-5049 (commit_to) are status 'planned' with contracts []. provium/src/coverage.rs:485-505 only checks that each ledger contract exists in its project. jarl/tests/proofs.rs:83-90 calls only that audit, so nothing checks that every project obligation appears in the ledger.","kind":"comment","references":"d9fc825098e182486a59f4bcc1b637b32be708233e95daffae90fab63cb4459a","summary":"confirmed: no coverage.json contract references proofs/consensus/project.json and the audit has no reverse check","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/coverage.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037852Z","id":"d7eb6b95f4e63547c572b516f56ea75163ab9a2e16a327446a00c3207223f458","body":{"detail":"src/state.rs:101 declares `pub(crate) fn write`. The coverage.json inventory marks it public=false, but entries[...State::write].root_apis (coverage.json:6946-6948) lists itself. State::full and State::get have root_apis []. A Python count over entries[*].root_apis gives 101 distinct roots: 100 public items plus crate::state::<State < V , S , CAP >>::write. M0.md:57 and M0.md:179 say 100 roots. provium/src/coverage.rs:479 checks only that public items list themselves.","kind":"comment","references":"7ef69833059093e882d9d62f301a9658327b00a4c35b9b425453d110928d73b4","summary":"confirmed: pub(crate) State::write lists itself in root_apis, giving 101 distinct roots against 100 public items","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037873Z","id":"f7104938f66e65c2ba8d87731c119bd6e5754617a2edc79d578ff59b0a25e62d","body":{"detail":"Grepping jarl/proofs/*/Proofs.lean finds majority_intersection only in consensus/Proofs.lean:43 and its use in joint_transition_intersection (:78-79). It quantifies over an abstract voters list and pure predicates, and the comment at :29-31 says the caller must connect them to the membership iterator. membership/Proofs.lean:1356-1366 Quorum.execution models a stateful callback σ threaded through countPredicates over the voters and then old_voters, but no Jarl theorem instantiates the intersection lemma with it. README.md:45 says 'actual shared-voter intersection'.","kind":"comment","references":"9cbf3f39811727289f76da69e7feabdcb8a71052ba2ccbd28be81d366687be40","summary":"confirmed: no theorem links majority_intersection to the generated Membership::quorum execution","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037893Z","id":"eff92cd38d00a23f88f7fc7b73c507205d256d25ac664970ec0de3dfea397df8","body":{"detail":"jarl/proofs/membership/project.json has 15 methods, including membership::Membership::quorum and quorum_index, and 114 obligations, 5 of them Quorum.* and 9 QuorumIndex.* (lines 424-476). README.md:49's membership row names finalized through joint but not quorum. `grep -n -i quorum jarl/proofs/README.md` matches only line 45, the consensus row.","kind":"comment","references":"4430a24908ed238aabb05172ac3a5d18f4a5b86d079ce12d13b3b59e6ecba43b","summary":"confirmed: the README membership row omits quorum and quorum_index","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037916Z","id":"5b99e697fc7355d558adf055c3bd4267f77eadfea7cffaaef5238c0aa086b810","body":{"detail":"storage/Proofs.lean:145: AppendHistory.fresh is ⟨List.replicate capacity none, 0⟩. :943-944: StorageHistory.fresh is the same buffer, with only `capacity < 2^bits`. state_State_new is linked only by the separate fresh_representation (:134-139). README.md:105-106 says the induction covers appends 'from the generated constructor'. The comment at :141-143 is accurate for AppendHistory itself. Its clause 'their preservation lemmas must be added before closing the storage invariant' is stale, because StorageHistory (:946-972) now has grow, truncate, install and restore constructors.","kind":"comment","references":"e7d5d47b26daff2abcc25be49a2925ce3b77456b248cb7ce0de0eb65d4817cba","summary":"confirmed: both history inductions start from a hand-written empty buffer, not from Jarl.state_State_new","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/PROGRESS.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037924Z","id":"7ce3b3eb0a2d7197e9e84e8d7bfba4248ae0af9fdd95600b97e18705f71a550c","body":{"detail":"PROGRESS.md:478 and :505 say storage has 44; jarl/proofs/storage/project.json has 53. PROGRESS.md:1269 and :1374 say membership has 111; membership/project.json has 114. PROGRESS.md:1384 says the host suite checks 267; the method projects (initialization 4, input-gating 8, log-boundary 12, membership 114, message-dispatch 2, message-validation 56, persistence 6, replication-contract 16, storage-view 13, storage 53) sum to 284. PROGRESS.md (1619 lines) never states 53, 114 or 284.","kind":"comment","references":"d55dce27be5044711f7028386f8ccf0e888084d3cf87eb534f03d909b3004e9d","summary":"confirmed: PROGRESS.md's latest counts (storage 44, membership 111, method suite 267) are older than the manifests (53, 114, 284)","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
